<title>JAPAN: Tokyo U.S. Treasury mkt closed for President&quot;s Day.</title>
<headline>Tokyo U.S. Treasury mkt closed for President&quot;s Day.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury market was closed in Tokyo on Monday for the President&quot;s Day holiday in the United States. Trade will resume on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Treasuries closed higher in New York on Friday as a friendly wholesale inflation report bolstered the market.</p>
<p>The key 30-year bond ended up 17/32 at 101-8/32, yielding 6.53 percent, in New York.</p>
</text>
